# rule.always.defer-fulcrums-to-last

a design fulcrum surfaces mid-drive: best-guess it, flag it, drive on. fulcrum review is one council at the very end.

| the fulcrum is | you |
|---|---|
| impliedly answered by the wish or a reviewer | take that answer — it was never a fulcrum |
| open, rework **clean** | best-guess, note why, flag for the end |
| open, rework **dirty** | `--as blocked` — last, and named |

**clean** = a rename, a swapped default, a re-scoped boundary that does not ripple.
**dirty** = callers hardened against it, or later work built upon it, so reversal is a teardown.
⚠️ the pair is `clean`/`dirty`, never `clean`/`not clean`.

unsure → treat it as clean and flag it. a flagged clean rework costs a glance; a premature block costs the road its momentum.

a block needs all three: no defensible guess · a dirty rework · every other question already addressed.

⇒ the RECORD half is `rule.always.itemize-the-fulcrums-you-best-guess`.
